// CRITICAL: All tests MUST be derived from battle-*.mdc rules in .cursor/rules/battle/
// These rules ARE the game mechanics - they define how the game actually works
// Each test MUST validate a specific rule's requirements

# 🚨 MANDATORY FIRST STEP 🚨
// BEFORE DOING ANYTHING ELSE:
// 1. RUN ALL TESTS
// 2. RECORD THE CURRENT FAILING TESTS
// 3. DOCUMENT THE FAILURE COUNT AND PATTERNS
// ⛔️ DO NOT PROCEED UNTIL THIS IS DONE ⛔️

# ⚠️ CRITICAL: KEEP TESTS SIMPLE AND FOCUSED ⚠️
// THE MOST IMPORTANT PRINCIPLE: Write the absolute minimum code needed
// DO NOT add complexity or try to be clever
// DO NOT try to handle edge cases not specified in the rules
// DO NOT add "nice to have" features
// JUST implement exactly what the rule requires - NOTHING MORE
// ALWAYS RUN A TEST TO SEE IF WE HAVE ANY FAILING AT THE START

# ⚠️ CRITICAL: TEST ISOLATION AND ORGANIZATION ⚠️
// @see @reactNativeLang/testing
// @see @jestLang/isolation
// @see @typescriptLang/testing-best-practices

1. Test Isolation Requirements
   - Each test MUST be completely independent
   - NEVER share mutable state between tests
   - Reset ALL mocks and spies in beforeEach/afterEach
   - Clear ALL timers and intervals after each test
   - Restore ALL modified globals after each test
   - Use unique test data per test case

2. Test Organization Standards
   - Group tests by feature/component/rule
   - Use descriptive test blocks (describe/context)
   - Follow naming pattern: "should <expected behavior> when <condition>"
   - Keep test files parallel to source files
   - Maximum test file size: 300 lines
   - Split large test suites into focused subsets

3. Mocking and Isolation Practices
   - Mock ALL external dependencies
   - Use dependency injection for better isolation
   - Create fresh mock instances per test
   - Never mock the system under test
   - Document ALL mock behaviors
   - Verify mock interactions explicitly

4. Debugging Support
   - Add meaningful test descriptions
   - Use clear failure messages
   - Log relevant state on failure
   - Maintain one assertion per test when possible
   - Include setup context in test names
   - Document complex test scenarios

# IMPORTANT!
   - CHECK YOUR CURRENT DIRECTORY BEFORE MAKING CHANGES

## Status Tracking
