Status: VERIFIED - All tests passing with comprehensive coverage of phase transitions, error handling, and state management

1. Write failing test first
   - Select rule from any [IN_PROGRESS] battle-*.mdc file in .cursor/rules/
   - Test MUST validate rule's specific requirements 
   - Rule being tested MUST be referenced in test
   - Test MUST validate actual game mechanics
   - Test MUST be as simple as possible - NO extra complexity
   - Update Status Tracking section after selection

2. Implement minimal code to pass
   - Write ONLY code needed to make test pass
   - NO extra features or optimizations
   - NO "future-proofing" or "just in case" code
   - Implementation MUST follow rule exactly
   - If it feels complex, you're doing too much
   - Keep it ruthlessly simple and focused

3. Run test suite
   - Verify ALL rule-based tests pass
   - Each battle-*.mdc rule MUST have coverage
   - Update source file's status if all tests for rule pass
   - If tests are complex, simplify them

4. Return to workflow
   - Move to performance check phase
   - Let workflow handle status updates
   - Remember: Simple tests are easier to maintain